---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import QuoteForm from "../../components/QuoteForm.astro";
import FAQ from "../../components/FAQ.astro";
import CTA from "../../components/CTA.astro";
import { serviceSchema } from "../../lib/schema";
import { SITE_URL, PRICE, SUBURBS, SERVICES, RE_INSPECTION_FEE, RE_INSPECTION_WINDOW_DAYS, GUARANTEE_FULL } from "../../config";

const service = SERVICES.find((s) => s.slug === "re-inspection")!;
const url = `${SITE_URL}/services/${service.slug}/`;
const linkedSuburbs = [
  SUBURBS.find((s) => s.slug === "bentleigh")!,
  SUBURBS.find((s) => s.slug === "caulfield")!,
  SUBURBS.find((s) => s.slug === "doncaster")!,
  SUBURBS.find((s) => s.slug === "templestowe")!,
  SUBURBS.find((s) => s.slug === "essendon")!,
  SUBURBS.find((s) => s.slug === "black-rock")!,
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "Is the re-inspection really free?",
    answer:
      `Your first re-inspection is free, provided it's a follow-up to an inspection you originally booked with us and it's booked within ${RE_INSPECTION_WINDOW_DAYS} days of that original visit. Outside that window, or for any additional re-inspection after that, the standard ${RE_INSPECTION_FEE} re-check fee applies.`,
  },
  {
    question: "How long do I have to fix issues before booking the re-inspection?",
    answer:
      `You have ${RE_INSPECTION_WINDOW_DAYS} days from your original inspection to get the identified issues fixed and your free re-inspection booked. We'd still recommend acting promptly — most repairs are quick — but that's the cut-off for the free follow-up to apply.`,
  },
  {
    question: "What if I was inspected by a different provider and failed?",
    answer:
      "We can still carry out your re-inspection, though it would be booked as a standard inspection at our usual flat fee rather than a free follow-up, since the original inspection wasn't through us.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do I need to prove the issues have been fixed before booking?",
    answer:
      "No — the re-inspection itself is how the fix gets confirmed. Just let us know the original issues have been addressed and we'll book the follow-up visit.",
  },
  {
    question: "What if my pool fails the re-inspection too?",
    answer:
      `Most properties pass on the second visit once the original issues are fixed — it's uncommon to fail twice. If it does happen, further re-inspections are ${RE_INSPECTION_FEE} each. Keep in mind the free re-check only applies to your first re-inspection, booked within ${RE_INSPECTION_WINDOW_DAYS} days of the original visit — every visit after that is charged at the standard re-check rate.`,
  },
];
---
<Layout
  title={service.metaTitle}
  description={service.metaDescription}
  path={`/services/${service.slug}/`}
  schema={[serviceSchema(service, url)]}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: "Services", path: "/services/" }, { name: service.name, path: `/services/${service.slug}/` }]} />

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-navy-900 mb-4 max-w-3xl">{service.h1}</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-navy-600 max-w-2xl mb-8">{service.summary}</p>

    <div class="prose-content max-w-3xl">
      <p>
        Failing a pool barrier inspection is a lot more common than most owners expect — around one in three
        barriers fail on the first visit. It's rarely a sign of anything seriously wrong; it's usually one or two
        specific, fixable issues that simply need to be corrected before a Form 23 Certificate of Barrier Compliance
        can be issued. The re-inspection is the follow-up visit that confirms those fixes and gets you across the
        line.
      </p>

      <h2>What typically needs fixing before a re-inspection</h2>
      <p>
        The most common items we see on a first-inspection report are straightforward: a gate hinge or self-closing
        spring that needs adjusting so the gate reliably closes and latches from any position; pot plants, furniture
        or garden features moved back from the non-climbable zone; a gap under the fence backfilled or fitted with
        infill; or overhanging branches trimmed back from the barrier line. Most of these are quick jobs for a
        handyperson or fencing contractor, often completed within a day or two.
      </p>

      <h2>How the re-inspection works</h2>
      <p>
        Once the issues from your original report have been addressed, get in touch to book your follow-up visit.
        Your inspector will specifically check the items identified in the first report, confirm they've been
        resolved, and reassess the barrier as a whole. If everything now meets the standard, your Form 23 is issued
        on the spot, the same as a first-time pass.
      </p>
    </div>

    <CTA
      heading="Book your free re-inspection"
      subtext={GUARANTEE_FULL}
    />

    <div class="prose-content max-w-3xl">
      <h2>Why the first re-inspection is included, not charged separately</h2>
      <p>
        Since roughly a third of barriers fail their first inspection, charging a full second call-out fee for what
        is often a very minor fix doesn't reflect how routine this outcome actually is. Our {PRICE} flat fee is
        structured with that in mind — it covers the original inspection and one free follow-up visit, provided
        repairs are made and the re-inspection is booked within {RE_INSPECTION_WINDOW_DAYS} days. Further visits
        after that are charged at {RE_INSPECTION_FEE} each, which covers the inspector's return trip and gives you
        a real incentive to get the fix right the first time rather than treat re-checks as unlimited.
      </p>

      <h2>If your first inspection wasn't with us</h2>
      <p>
        We can still carry out a re-inspection if a different provider assessed your barrier initially. In that
        case, it's treated as a standard inspection at our usual {PRICE} flat fee, since the free re-inspection
        guarantee applies specifically to inspections originally booked through us.
      </p>

      <h2>Pricing</h2>
      <p>
        {GUARANTEE_FULL} Re-inspections following another provider's original inspection are charged at our
        standard {PRICE} flat rate. See our <a href="/pricing/">full pricing breakdown</a> for more detail.
      </p>

      <h2>Related guides</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/guides/what-fails-pool-inspection/">What fails a pool inspection in Victoria</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/pool-inspection-cost-melbourne/">How much a Melbourne pool inspection costs</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/four-year-reinspection-cycle/">The four-year re-inspection cycle explained</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Available across Melbourne</h2>
      <p>We carry out re-inspections across the metro area, including:</p>
      <ul class="columns-2 sm:columns-3">
        {linkedSuburbs.map((s) => (
          <li><a href={`/locations/${s.slug}/`}>Re-inspections {s.name}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p><a href="/locations/">See all service areas &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>

    <div id="quote-form" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto my-12">
      <QuoteForm />
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <FAQ faqs={faqs} heading="Frequently asked questions about re-inspections" />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
